<h1>About Prayerbook Atlas</h1>
<hr class="title-rule">

<p>
  Prayerbook Atlas is for Anglican and Episcopal common prayer across the Books of Common Prayer.
  It sets each book before you on its own terms: its text, rubrics, calendar, and lectionary as
  printed, with the book, printing, and page beside every text.
</p>

<p>
  It is personal lay work and the sister project of
  <a href="https://graceandfootnotes.com">Grace &amp; Footnotes</a>. It is not an official
  publication of the Church of England, The Episcopal Church, the Anglican Church in North
  America, the Anglican Communion, or any other church, diocese, or parish, and it does not speak
  for any of them.
</p>

<p>
  It collects nothing about you: no analytics, advertising, or tracking. It sets only its own
  strictly necessary cookies: one that protects its forms, and, if you choose between the phone
  site and the full site, one that remembers that choice.
</p>

<p>
  Write to <a href="mailto:support@prayerbookatlas.com">support@prayerbookatlas.com</a>.
</p>
